It broke because the `build` fixture in arrt/tests/unit/test_look.py names the picture store's temporary files with a Python generator expression (`staged = (f\"{n:08x}\" for n in itertools.count())`, passed as `staging_token=lambda: next(staged)`). LookService fetches missing pictures on a ThreadPoolExecutor with one worker per picture (look.py, `max_workers=len(missing)`), and each fetch reaches `PictureStore._write` -> `self._staging_token()`. A generator re-entered from a second thread while the first is suspended inside its frame (the GIL can be handed over at the generator's RESUME) raises `ValueError: generator already executing`. `PictureStore.keep` catches only `_NotKept`, so the ValueError escapes `_fetched` (which catches only ServiceError) into a future nobody reads, and the picture is never kept. `test_the_model_s_look_stays_within_its_budget_and_says_what_it_left_for_later` fetches two pictures concurrently with equal sleeps, then asserts `set(later.previews) == {every picture}`, so it can fail at random on a loaded runner. Production is not affected, because its default is `uuid.uuid4().hex`. The fix: build the token from a C-level counter, as `counted_tokens()` in test_pictures.py already does (`counter = itertools.count(); lambda: f\"{next(counter):08x}\"`). A call to `next()` on `itertools.count` is atomic under the GIL. Or reuse that helper. I checked the other injected token and id callables this diff adds: fakes.counted_ids, test_backup_writer.ticking_names, test_pictures.counted_tokens, and the `iter([...]).__next__` uses. All are C-level iterators or single-threaded, so this is the only one.", "files": ["arrt/tests/unit/test_look.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Counter-based id and staging-token helpers reimplemented per test file instead of one owner beside open_catalogue in fakes.py", "recommendation": "Scope: class. It broke because the branch gave the catalogue opener a shared owner (fakes.open_catalogue and counted_ids) but gave the picture store none, so each converted file wrote its own copy. arrt/tests/unit/test_default_theme_migration.py `_IDS`/`_an_id` has the same body as fakes.counted_ids (`str(uuid.UUID(int=next(counter)))`) in a file that already imports from fakes. The PictureStore staging token is written three ways: test_pictures.py `counted_tokens`, test_backup_writer.py `ticking_names`, and an inline generator in test_look.py's `build` fixture. Only 4 of the roughly 13 `PictureStore(` construction sites under arrt/tests pass `staging_token`. test_previews, test_phase_two_run, test_run_citations, test_offered_works, test_resolve_run and test_sightings still draw uuid4 on every write. Whoever converts them next will copy a fourth variant or leave the token out without noticing, since nothing reports a test that silently became uncacheable. Fix: use fakes.counted_ids in test_default_theme_migration.py. Add one test factory for a cache-safe PictureStore to fakes.py next to `open_catalogue` (fixed `now`, counted `staging_token`) and route the three sites through it. Then `grep -rn 'PictureStore(' arrt/tests` is the checklist for the rest.", "files": ["arrt/tests/fakes.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_default_theme_migration.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_pictures.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_backup_writer.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_look.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "blocking", "title": "record-lint chunk-ref-missing: chunk 01:52", "recommendation": "(1) declared deliverable `tests/repository.py:projects` file does not exist; (2) declared deliverable `tests/preferences/test_citations_resolve.py:_tracked` file does not exist", "source": "record-lint", "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "blocking", "title": "record-lint chunk-ref-missing: chunk 02:62", "recommendation": "declared deliverable `persistence/kept.py` file does not exist", "source": "record-lint", "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is 